<title>USA: National Patent adopts rights plan.</title>
<headline>National Patent adopts rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Patent Development Corp said Tuesday it adopted a shareholders right plan with a 20 percent trigger.</p>
<p>The company said it knew of no proposed or threatened takeover, tender offer or other effort to gain control of the company and said the plan was not intended to prevent an acquisition on terms favorable to stockholders.  </p>
<p>National Patent said preferred share purchase rights distributed under the plan will be exercised and trade separately from the common shares only if a person or group acquires beneficial ownership of 20 percent or more of its shares. The rights expire July 3, 2007, it said.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
